<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK UTILITY POSTS LOWER 9MO NET PROFIT.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK UTILITY POSTS LOWER 9MO NET PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for nine-month period</p>
<p>ending September 30, 1996: (in billion crowns)</p>
<p> After-tax profit			2.559	     5.181</p>
<p> Operating revenues		   21.334	    18.794</p>
<p> Operating costs			16.204	    11.621</p>
<p> Operating profit			5.129	     7.173</p>
<p> Profit from regular activities    2.571	     5.149</p>
<p>Revenues from financial</p>
<p>  operations			     0.362	     0.076</p>
<p> Financial costs			 0.894	     0.704</p>
<p>Results from financial</p>
<p>  operations			    -0.532	    -0.628</p>
<p> Total loans			    26.101	    16.305</p>
<p> Long-term loans			21.711	    11.601</p>
<p> Short-term loans			4.390	     4.703</p>
<p> Reserves				  0.357	     0.018</p>
<p> Basic capital			  41.804	    40.289</p>
<p> Total assets			   87.087	    78.815</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Slovenske Elektrarne a.s. (SE).</p>
<p>All figures are in positive terms except where indicated.</p>
<p>Results are provided by the Bratislava Stock Exchange. SE is a</p>
<p>wholly state-owned energy monopoly. It is included on the</p>
<p>government's list of strategic companies excluded from</p>
<p>privatisation.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-563-3688</p>
</text>
